are you thinking what i think you're  thinking i'm thinking it what are we  thinking thinking we're taking it too  the hotly anticipated sequel to thor  ragnarok thor love and thunder made fans  bang their proverbial hammers with  excitement here's a looky-loo to see all  the chaos and fun that surrounded the  making of the marvel flick  number one  that's gotta hurt while it's no secret  that any actor called upon to take a  marvel movie leading role is going to  have to get into some kind of  over-the-top muscular shape all that  weightlifting can come at a cost chris  hemsworth as thor learned the hard way  by wrecking his back mid-thor love and  thunder while the exact injury and  circumstances surrounding it are still  shrouded in mystery hemsworth had to  injure cortisol injections to keep  holding up that hammer  number 2  ouch adapting a beloved comic book hero  onto the big screen is no small feat  and unfortunately sometimes characters  get the boot e tree played by peter  dinklage sadly didn't make the cut this  time  however christian bale who plays the  main villain gore the godbutcher said he  treasured his time on set with dinklage  the other character who the editor of  thor had to say  sorry not sorry to was the grandmaster  played by everyone's favorite rambling  actor jeff goldblum it's safe to say  that we demand a buddy comedy spin-off  featuring dinklage and goldblum thank  you  number three  it's getting spicy now the moment that  all fan fiction writers and weirdos were  asking for finally made an appearance in  thor love and thunder thor's nude  physique and when nudity is called for  in a feature film it tends to be dealt  tenderly and privately according to  director taiko ititi there were over 350  people on set that day most of whom had  never spent one day on the set before or  after the entire shoot here's hoping  chris wasn't too cold that day number  four  can't stop won't stop director taika ytt  may have won an academy award for  writing his movie jojo rabbit but his  real skill is making the actors do the  make-em-ups showcased in his movie what  we do in the shadows his flair for  improv is unmatched and great news is  his directing style allowed actors like  chris hemsworth to improvise some  hilarious moments that fans will love  hemsworth explained it's free form  there's a lot of improvisation that's  just an unrivaled passion there was an  enthusiasm that was infectious among  everybody  number five  get ready to dance marvel movies have  found a way to impact all levels of the  entertainment industry especially the  music world with soundtracks like  guardians of the galaxy making gen z  kids groove to the 70s hits director  taika ytti hopes to hit the same notes  in his choice of 80s classics waititi  said he spent his youth obsessed with  bands like guns n roses and metallica  and is so thrilled they were able to  make it into thor love and thunder  because nothing says superhero quite  like a seven minute slash guitar solo  number six  was gore the god but you're going to be  the lord of the dance while many rumors  have come out of thor love and thunder  one that fans were desperate to be true  was christian balesville and gore the  god butcher having a full dance scene to  a kate bush song and while the scene was  never actually filmed it was according  to bale vividly discussed but some  dreams never do make it to the big  screen and watching a grotesque bale  dance to babushka can only live in our  heads  number seven  get ready for mighty thor  after years of mostly male superheroes  thor love and thunder finally is  allowing the girl character to become  three-dimensional and cause all the  drama natalie portman who plays jane  foster steps into thor's very large  shoes and gets to strut her stuff as a  god and hero portman elaborated on this  exciting opportunity saying getting this  opportunity was such an incredible way  to explore a female superhero that could  be quite vulnerable and weak find  strength in that and be more like a  human i could relate to personally thank  goodness her costume wasn't all pink  number eight  and the chaos continues no matter how  much chaos and excitement there already  is behind the scenes sometimes it's nice  to have family around so for all you  cameo heads keep your eyes open for  chris hemsworth's real-life wife and  children to make an appearance tbh on a  movie like this the more chaos the  better so the kids brought it number  nine  most movies need a big star to get off  the ground however when you have a  built-in fan base like a marvel  franchise that may not always be the  case but this time chris hemsworth made  this fourth thor movie happen because of  how damn hilarious he is according to  ytt chris showed off his comedic chops  in avengers age of ultron and made the  studios decide that yeah they do want to  see a comedy version of thor and  thankfully fans do too number 10  what's that christian bale is a  sought-after actor with both box office  and critical success so choosing him to  play the villain gore the godbutcher was  a no-brainer and while bale is known to  transform himself both through his  acting and his literal body also known  as how extremely thin he got in the  machinist he couldn't go the extra mile  body wise this time if fans recall gore  is a big hulky dude and in thor love and  thunder he's definitely leaned out this  was due to bale coming off of another  project where he needed to be thinner  maybe a first of hollywood not wanting  someone to be thinner for a role number  11.  we'd pass on this ever since gwyneth  group paltrow introduced the world to  the wim hof method hollywood has been  dipping their toes into ice baths and  while this is a long practice tradition  by all top grade athletes the cast of  thor gave it a go as well having the  actors reinvigorate their tense muscles  with an ice bath is literally what the  doctor ordered number 12.  we gotta talk about the goats in thor  love and thunder goats play a prominent  role um fun and while these ones were  all cgi the actors had to stare and  react at something for acting's sake so  they brought in the goat sculptures  no word on how realistic they were but  here's hoping they look as ridiculous as  they must have felt to act against a  sculpture number 13. the original cut of  thor love and thunder was just over four  hours according to hemsworth who called  it an assembly of madness fans should be  relieved that the theatrical version is  much much shorter however it would have  been pretty cool to see a 20-minute  scene of thor's morning routine  number 14.  romance is in the air if upon watching  thor love and thunder you can't help but  think you've seen certain images in  print form ever so slightly concealed on  your mom's nightstand you're right for  having this feeling director taika ytt  based his cinematography choices on the  harlequin romance novel aesthetic based  on publishing house mills and boone  moments in the movie and right down to  the poster why tt wanted the feeling of  flowing hair beauties and billowy shirts  one can only find in a drugstore book  section fingers crossed for a fabio  cameo someday number 15.  who would have thought marvel movies  tend to steer clear from any sort of  romantic storyline as if it were  kryptonite itself oops wrong comic book  franchise but thor love and thunder  leans right into the romance in fact  categorizing itself as a romantic comedy  director taika waititi even said he was  inspired by the rom-com an officer and a  gentleman  well then if it's color we need  let's bring the rainbow  hope you had fun walking through the  chaos and madness that was the  behind-the-scenes antics of thor love  and thunder which behind the scene  tidbit tickled your fancy like comment  and subscribe to the things for all the  thor you can hammer we mean handle

